  "summary": "Dieselpunk's glamorous sibling: chrome ziggurats instead of rust and grease.",
  "description": "Decopunk is the art-deco-leaning, cleaner-surfaced branch of the retrofuture family: ziggurat skyscrapers, sunburst grilles, lacquered chrome, illuminated theater marquees and the sort of gleaming metropolis Metropolis and the Chrysler Building promised. Where dieselpunk goes grimy and military, decopunk stays dressed for the premiere — polish, glamour, symmetry, stepped ornamentation. Its canon includes Bioshock Infinite's Columbia lighter modes, Batman: The Animated Series' deco-noir, and The Rocketeer; collectors point to Coney Island's Parachute Jump and Radio City interiors as ground truth for the style's geometry.",
  "culturalContext": "Decopunk is dieselpunk's glamorous art-deco branch: chrome ziggurats, lacquer, marquees and the metropolis Metropolis promised. Batman: The Animated Series and The Rocketeer canonized its polish-and-symmetry — futurism dressed for the premiere rather than the factory floor.",
